  "narration": {
    "script": "You're in a rush, you grab your seatbelt, yank\u2014 and it locks up. Clank. Clank. Clank. Annoying, right? But that is exactly what could save your life. In a crash, your body lurches forward fast. So your seatbelt is designed to lock when the belt gets pulled too suddenly. Inside the retractor, a fast jerk triggers a locking mechanism that stops the belt from feeding out. No lock? You fly forward. With the lock\u2014 the belt catches you instantly. And you are now much safer.",
    "voice": {
      "profile": "hold-up-narrator"
    },
